#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# kde-rice: rice-ctl - one control point for every rice feature (backend of the Rice Center app).
#   rice-ctl list [--json]            every feature with its live state
#   rice-ctl get <id>                 one feature (JSON)
#   rice-ctl on|off <id>              turn a feature on / off (prints the feature as JSON)
#   rice-ctl set <id> <value>         choose a value (choice features)
#   rice-ctl set <id> <key> <value>   change a setting of a feature
#   rice-ctl action <id> <action> [arg]   run an action (snapshot, restore, doctor, ...)
#   rice-ctl help <id>                that feature's section of ~/kde-rice/USAGE.md
#   rice-ctl look rice|stock|original [--layout]   switch the whole look (reversible, snapshot first)
# Every change uses the documented on/off commands of the rice (USAGE.md / BACKUP-RESTORE.md).
# sudo is never run silently: such actions open Konsole so the password prompt is visible.
